pBb0_vybkBGAPFAYKgprxs2qX_672mbSNkiSKFLCwgZFqbWtdgpDLCTxpwPTvGBctguK6uZAs41vZDUeHevCHhNtZ6L0z9IKzX0LSQDS2H-_fyofXkZ7G_MMIL8ZgZZncZSyixNce3cLkpggs-PFb8eRulYa3_sHjJN5ZYfNxOu0f14GbroBtnYh3vy7mP2v0PhFEdydBsknUXygva_ubDOC6gZoHGHtPcu4h3IpUfKjB_s1sa5kZ7s8tUau3vxRf61BocU_X5RINN4SLWZirpegNCp9tHfevPfMNiE5zVV_IwMsqVfo_DshwXVkqDuiScm6Fkhjk_yRaAT-RskLzkypSV3yHbdlbeTXTb0_z_2Y4H8tkb0_mbmo8qE0te86d5mc="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_041377e3fb4dfead016adb0ae3b6508191b708f2bce74ff34d","call_id":"call_db282e6aac504220b5d611d14b7b7827","name":"check_artifact","arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"spec\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"lie-module-irreducibility\\\",\\\"full_target\\\":\\\"For every prime p, field K of characteristic p, integer λ with 0 ≤ λ < p, and admissible lattice M in V(λ), M⊗_Z K is irreducible for L(K).\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"For every prime p, field K of characteristic p, integer λ with 0 ≤ λ < p, and admissible lattice M in V(λ), M⊗_Z K is irreducible for L(K).\\\",\\\"parameters\\\":[],\\\"hypotheses\\\":[],\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"logic\\\":{\\\"classical\\\":true,\\\"rules\\\":[],\\\"calculations\\\":[\\\"Finite algebra and localization calculations\\\"],\\\"primitives\\\":[]},\\\"pins\\\":{\\\"lean_version\\\":\\\"4.32.2\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"/Users/syyui/formalization-tools/lean-mathlib-v4.32.2/mathlib\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"lie-module-irreducibility\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For every prime p, field K of characteristic p, integer λ with 0 ≤ λ < p, and admissible lattice M in V(λ), M⊗_Z K is irreducible for L(K).\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"rules\\\":[],\\\"locals\\\":[],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary p,K,λ,M satisfying the target. Write R=Z_(p), choose the standard basis e_i=y^i v_+/i! (0≤i≤λ) of V(λ), and write X_r=x^r/r!, Y_r=y^r/r!. The sl2 relations and highest-weight equations give X_r e_i=binom(λ-i+r,r)e_(i-r), Y_r e_i=binom(i+r,r)e_(i+r), with out-of-range terms zero. Thus the operators are integral in this basis. Localize M to M_R=R⊗_Z M. Admissibility makes it stable under X_r,Y_r. The matrix-unit operators satisfy Y_λX_λ=E_λλ, X_(λ-i)E_λλ=E_iλ, and E_λλY_(λ-j)=binom(λ,j)E_λj. Because λ<p, all binom(λ,j) are units of R, hence each E_ij=E_iλE_λj lies in the localized operator algebra and preserves M_R. Define J_i={c∈C:c e_i∈M_R}. Since E_ii projects M_R onto J_i e_i and M_R is finite over R, J_i is finite over R; it is nonzero since M_R spans V(λ) over C. E_ij and E_ji imply J_i=J_j; call this common module J. The projections sum to the identity, so M_R=⊕_{i=0}^λ J e_i. M_R is free of rank λ+1 over R, whence J is finite torsion-free of rank one. Explicitly, choose a nonzero a∈J; rank one means every element of J is a rational multiple of a. Finite generation gives a finite set of rational multipliers; taking their minimum p-adic valuation shows J=bR for some b∈C, so J is free rank one. (This also covers λ=0.) The isomorphism R→J identifies M_R with the standard module in the basis b e_i and intertwines x,y,h. Reduction modulo p identifies M_R/pM_R with the standard module over F_p, and extension of scalars identifies it with M⊗_Z K. Since r! is invertible modulo p for r≤λ, the divided powers X_r,Y_r on this module are scalar multiples of x^r,y^r. The matrix-unit identities therefore show that the algebra generated by x,y contains every E_ij, including when p=2. A submodule W is stable under these operators. If w=Σ c_i e_i∈W is nonzero, choose c_i≠0; then E_ji w=c_i e_j for every j, so W contains every basis vector and equals the module. The dimension λ+1 is positive. This proves irreducibility for every admissible lattice and all stated parameters.\\\" ,\\\"uses\\\":[],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[]}]}}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Stop this stage honestly on a substantive or suspected proof gap, unavailable source, or input conflict. JSON fields: status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. Status must be SUBSTANTIVE_GAP, SUSPECTED_GAP, SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT. Difficulty alone is not a mathematical error.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"12602acb-3f01-49e2-b2c0-02d51fbf7178","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26036,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1191,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":137},"total_tokens":27227,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_041377e3fb4dfead016adb0a842e408191b589a8ad15e1bcaf":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_041377e